            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AZ93"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were so good! I made them with and without refried beans added and made my own salsa. For my cheddar I used applewood smoked cheddar inside and on top, and the flavor it added was amazing. I highly recommend using a smoked cheese with it. After baking I broiled the enchiladas for a couple of minutes to lightly brown the top. So yummy, and very easy to prep. Served with spanish rice and paired it with \"A big honkin' margarita\" from this site. great mexican dinner night!! Can't wait to make these again. Thanks bean machine!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Hunter Louis Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "You can't really go wrong here... Mine were crammed in as I didn't have 8\" tortillas on hand-- only the larger and no onions! Ugh. Haha. But it still turned out great. The only changes I made: with the cheese mixture I added some onion powder, onion and herb blend, and red pepper flakes.) A dash cayenne or chili powder wouldn't hurt depending on your tastes... Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-07T16:10:02.100Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "the4taals"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My husband loves cheese enchiladas, this recipe was very easy and tasty. I scaled to 20 servings as I had 20 tortillas to use. I omitted the green onions and substituted drained chopped spinach, I also made enchilada sauce for the top instead of using salsa. I used nacho cheese blend for the shredded cheese instead of each individual type. Needed more than 20 minutes to melt the cheese properly, more like 30 minutes would be better.",
            "datePublished": "2022-10-31T16:50:36.130Z"
          },
          {
